  "term": "blood poisoning",
  "definition": "Blood poisoning is an older term for septicemia, a serious condition in which disease-causing microorganisms enter the bloodstream and trigger a fast-moving whole-body reaction that can progress to shock. It commonly involves fever, chills, a fast heart rate, and rapid breathing, and it is a medical emergency.",
